    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "In the first deal, the holder of highest double leads it as the center. In later deals, the designated starting player may lead any double; if none, they pass and turn continues until someone leads a double. Each player has a personal train extending from the center. On turn, a player must play if legal. A legal play is usually to own train, but a player may instead play to another player's train only if that owner previously passed and the end has not changed since that pass. When a player passes, their train is open. If another player adds a non-double to that open train, it becomes private again. Play ends when a player empties hand or everyone is blocked.",
    Player: "In the first deal, the holder of highest double leads it as the center. In later deals, the designated starting player may lead any double; if none, they pass and turn continues until someone leads a double. Each player has a personal train extending from the center. On turn, a player must play if legal. A legal play is usually to own train, but a player may instead play to another player's train only if that owner previously passed and the end has not changed since that pass. When a player passes, their train is open. If another player adds a non-double to that open train, it becomes private again. Play ends when a player empties hand or everyone is blocked.",
    objective: 'Play all tiles first, or in a blocked hand have the lowest pip total on unplayed tiles.',
    gameplay: "In the first deal, the holder of highest double leads it as the center. In later deals, the designated starting player may lead any double; if none, they pass and turn continues until someone leads a double. Each player has a personal train extending from the center. On turn, a player must play if legal. A legal play is usually to own train, but a player may instead play to another player's train only if that owner previously passed and the end has not changed since that pass. When a player passes, their train is open. If another player adds a non-double to that open train, it becomes private again. Play ends when a player empties hand or everyone is blocked.",
    keyRules: [
      'If a legal tile exists on any currently legal train, passing is not allowed.',
      'Open-train status is tied to pass state and can close again when its end changes.',
      'In blocked hands, lowest pip total wins; if two or more tie for least spots, there is no winner and no one scores.',
      'Session end is by agreed deal count or agreed target score.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 to 4 players; four-player is the base form.',
      deck: 'One double-six domino set of 28 tiles.',
      equipment: 'Optional train markers to show which trains are open after a pass.',
      dealing: 'Deal 7 tiles to each player. In 4-player games all tiles are dealt. In 3-player games one 7-tile heap remains face down. In 2-player games two 7-tile heaps remain face down.',
    },
    turnFlow: "In the first deal, the holder of highest double leads it as the center. In later deals, the designated starting player may lead any double; if none, they pass and turn continues until someone leads a double. Each player has a personal train extending from the center. On turn, a player must play if legal. A legal play is usually to own train, but a player may instead play to another player's train only if that owner previously passed and the end has not changed since that pass. When a player passes, their train is open. If another player adds a non-double to that open train, it becomes private again. Play ends when a player empties hand or everyone is blocked.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Garrafina uses score settlement per deal, not ante betting.',
      deal: 'Dealer action at the start of each deal.',
      reveal_market: 'Garrafina has no market zone.',
      buy_market: 'No market purchases exist in Garrafina rules.',
      buy_stock: 'Only on first turn, only if exchange heap is still available, and according to variant-specific conditions.',
      fold: 'Garrafina has no fold mechanic; players must play or pass legally.',
      check: 'No betting rounds exist in Garrafina.',
      call: 'No betting rounds exist in Garrafina.',
      bet: 'Scoring is point accounting, not betting.',
      raise: 'Scoring is point accounting, not betting.',
      declare: 'There is no declaration phase in Garrafina.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands remain hidden until deal resolution.',
      award_pot: 'Resolution phase only.',
      play_card: 'Tile must match the active train end; if a legal play exists, passing is forbidden.',
      draw: 'Standard Garrafina has no boneyard draw; only Correlativa variant adds drawing.',
      discard: 'Variant-specific exchange only; discarded hand stays out of play.',
      pass: 'Illegal if any legal play exists.',
      bid: 'Garrafina has no bidding system.',
      meld: 'Garrafina is a connection domino game, not a meld game.',
      go_out: 'Occurs immediately after the player places last tile.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 7 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Play all tiles first, or in a blocked hand have the lowest pip total on unplayed tiles.',
      "Turn-flow example: In the first deal, the holder of highest double leads it as the center. In later deals, the designated starting player may lead any double; if none, they pass and turn continues until someone leads a double. Each player has a personal train extending from the center. On turn, a player must play if legal. A legal play is usually to own train, but a player may instead play to another player's train only if that owner previously passed and the end has not changed since that pass. When a player passes, their train is open. If another player adds a non-double to that open train, it becomes private again. Play ends when a player empties hand or everyone is blocked.",
      "Scoring example: When someone goes out, each loser loses points equal to pips left in hand and winner gains their sum. In blocked hands, each loser loses the difference between their pips and the winner's pips; winner gains sum of losses. Win each deal by going out first or having the lowest pip total when blocked; win session by agreed deal count or reaching agreed target..",
